@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+# Desktop note count
+
+The existing command manifest and local capability explicitly allow only `count_notes` alongside the original note commands. The Desktop count indicator calls `count_notes` in Rust and announces the result through a polite, atomic status region. Successful add/delete operations refresh it. Success payloads pass through the shared integer count schema. Invalid success payloads or native state/transport failures show an unavailable count and a keyboard-accessible retry; failures never display a fabricated zero or clear saved notes. There is no automatic retry.
+
+The implementation follows the existing pinned Tauri API 2.12.2/native Tauri 2.12.2 and React 19.3.0 contracts. Official [Tauri command guidance](https://v2.tauri.app/develop/calling-rust/), [native testing guidance](https://v2.tauri.app/develop/tests/webdriver/), [React Effect cleanup](https://react.dev/reference/react/useEffect) and [status semantics](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Accessibility/ARIA/Reference/Roles/status_role) were read on 2026-10-12 UTC. Compatibility is established by the recorded targeted tests and actual target-OS native gates, not by documentation retrieval alone.
+
+The independent rehearsal starts from generated source origin `0f9611c1c8e6934aa3f8d0fce924bcc9f4da9d5d`, content ID `8d37cdc64694fb9997fd60c5df10bd412a18695ebb63480f2fd148363e835628`. It accesses this generated project and its own disposable `codex/agent-desktop-99c` branch/run artifacts only. `Quality` has an explicit `agent_desktop` dispatch input for this generated project; default dispatch, PR and main behavior retain the original workflow. The independent path runs the unchanged selected Desktop full gate and the standard pre-PR/CI entries on actual Linux/macOS/Windows runners, plus native development startup, unsigned build and deployment preflight. It does not represent the source template's complete cross-preset acceptance matrix.
+
+Renderer tests cover count updates, accessibility, retry, invalid payloads and IPC failure. Native Rust tests cover current state and poisoned-lock error projection; native-window tests invoke real count IPC and mutations, including rejected malformed command arguments. All original test assertions, deadlines, quality definitions, release isolation and failure severities remain active. Logs and per-command exit/timing/source identity reports are retained under `artifacts/agent-desktop` even on failure. Git commit/push use the generated project's repository-local hooks. No signing, distribution, PR, merge, production deployment or protection changes are part of this rehearsal.
+
+Development evidence distinguishes native startup/cleanup completion from the deliberately stopped process's exit code and signal.
+
+The specialized hosted checkout requests the exact dispatched feature commit and only its bounded independent ancestry. It does not fetch other branches or canonical repository history. Existing default CI checkout behavior remains unchanged.
+
+The specialized runner sets TMPDIR, TMP and TEMP to its project-owned `.state/tmp`, including Windows Node/Rust temp selection. Support command records preserve these environment paths.
